{
  "_what": "Curated high-confidence psychiatric / neurodevelopmental risk-gene -> disorder map. This is the human-curated, LITERATURE-CITED INPUT to the gene-verification atlas (module DGENE, v1.28). Each gene is fetched VERBATIM from NCBI RefSeq (GRCh38) by the locked SantaLucia-1998 nearest-neighbour pipeline (the SAME read-only metric used by DNA M0 / neuro / mind M9) to record its promoter gamma with full provenance + sequence sha256. NOTHING here is a causal model: these disorders are POLYGENIC and HETEROGENEOUS (the >270-loci / SFARI-1000+ / DDG2P reality is LOCKED), and this is a curated HIGH-CONFIDENCE SUBSET, not an exhaustive list. The atlas makes the cited gene LOCKs of the D-series modules REPRODUCIBLE and VERIFIED; it asserts nothing about felt experience and is NOT medical advice.",
  "_grading": "gene identity + promoter gamma = [F] measured/reproducible (fetched verbatim, sequence sha256 recorded); disorder assignment + functional class = [cited]; polygenicity/heterogeneity + non-causality = [LOCK]; any gamma structure across the set = [O] honest characterisation, never a target.",
